= Classification =

V2 separates classification dimensions instead of encoding them all as categories.

== Namespace ==
Namespaces represent system roles: knowledge, users, project/meta documentation, templates, modules, semantic properties, files, help, and other MediaWiki-native concerns.

== Entity type ==
Entity type answers: '''what kind of thing is this page about?'''

The vocabulary should remain small and evidence-driven. Candidate types include concept, theory, model, method, project, implementation, organization, person, publication, dataset, software, protocol, species, and technology.

== Domain ==
Domain answers: '''what field or body of knowledge does this belong to?'''

Examples include systems science, biology, computer science, mathematics, philosophy, economics, physics, engineering, and environmental science. Pages may belong to multiple domains.

== Scope ==
Scope is optional. It describes a real applicability boundary such as geography, time, jurisdiction, system boundary, experimental context, or level of analysis. It should not be populated merely because a schema allows it.

== Categories and properties ==
Use categories for meaningful human groupings and navigation. Use semantic properties for attributes and relationships of individual pages. Do not create a category merely to mirror every property value.

